1
00:00:00,781 --> 00:00:02,411
- Raj?
- No way, Jose.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:06,450
- But I can't do it. I can't see anything.
- It's all right.

3
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:09,250
(Howard:)Wireless mini-cam
and Bluetooth headset.

4
00:00:09,414 --> 00:00:11,874
(Howard:)We'll be your eyes.

5
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:14,880
- Fine.
- One more thing.

6
00:00:15,253 --> 00:00:19,593
(Howard:)This is a sub-sonic impact sensor.

7
00:00:19,758 --> 00:00:21,968
(Howard:)If Sheldon gets out of bed
and starts to walk...

8
00:00:22,135 --> 00:00:24,765
...this will register it
and send a signal to the laptop.

9
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:28,720
(Howard:)At that point, based on the geography of
the apartment and the speed of Sheldon...

10
00:00:28,892 --> 00:00:32,432
(Howard:)...you'll have seven seconds to get out,
glasses or no glasses.

11
00:00:32,604 --> 00:00:34,314
(Leonard:)Won't my footsteps set it off?

12
00:00:34,481 --> 00:00:36,861
(Howard:)No. You'll be on your hands and knees.

13
00:00:37,025 --> 00:00:39,775
(Howard:)Now, you'll need to get the sensor
close to Sheldon's room.

14
00:00:39,945 --> 00:00:42,575
(Leonard:)How do I carry it
if I'm on my hands and knees?

15
00:00:47,953 --> 00:00:49,413
HOWARD:
Stay low.

16
00:00:49,996 --> 00:00:51,376
(Howard:)Bear left.

17
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:53,580
(Howard:)- Now keep true.
- What?

18
00:00:53,750 --> 00:00:56,920
- It means go straight.
- Then just say, "Go straight."

19
00:00:57,420 --> 00:01:01,260
You don't say, "Go straight," when you're
giving bearings. You say, "Keep true."

